===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|mansion}}{{lb|en|now|chiefly|historical}} A large [[town house]] or [[mansion]]; a grand private [[residence]], especially in France. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Wharton Age of Innocence|chapter=2|text= [T]he cream-coloured house (supposed to be modelled on the private '''hotels''' of the Parisian aristocracy) was there[.]}}
# {{senseid|en|Q27686}}An [[establishment]] that provides [[accommodation]] and other services for paying guests; normally larger than a [[guesthouse]], and often one of a [[chain]]. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#* '''1868''', "A Clergyman" (John Morison), ''Australia in 1866'', [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=hvQNAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA165&dq=%22hotel%22|%22hotels%22+australia+OR+zealand+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=2SmIT93qA-qhiAezqMDTCQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22hotel%22|%22hotels%22%20australia%20OR%20zealand%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false page 165],
#*: When gold-digging commenced in California, the writer was staying at an '''hotel''' in Wellington, New Zealand, where a Yankee trader was also staying. Seated at the dining-table, the latter was discoursing of the business he was doing{{...}}.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-29|volume=407|issue=8842|page=28|magazine=w:The Economist
|titleurl=http://www.economist.com/news/asia/21580209-natural-disaster-aggravated-poor-response-high-and-wet|title=High and wet
|passage=Floods in northern India, mostly in the small state of Uttarakhand, have wrought disaster on an enormous scale. The early, intense onset of the monsoon on June 14th swelled rivers, washing away roads, bridges, '''hotels''' and even whole villages. Rock-filled torrents smashed vehicles and homes, burying victims under rubble and sludge.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20201101175949/https://www.economist.com/asia/2013/06/29/high-and-wet}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Dan Heching, Manuela Castro, Mauricio Torres, Alli Rosenbloom and Christian Edwards|title=Liam Payne, former One Direction member, dies after hotel balcony fall|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/16/entertainment/liam-payne-death-one-direction|date=2024-10-16|passage=Liam Payne, a former member of the boyband One Direction, has died after falling from the third floor of a '''hotel''' in Buenos Aires, Argentina, according to local police. Payne, who was 31, leaves behind his seven-year-old son, Bear.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250226124457/https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/16/entertainment/liam-payne-death-one-direction/}}
